>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must not have boolean dtype to avoid “Bool inputs not supported”)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor must not have complex dtype to avoid “clamp is not supported for complex types”)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10)
>>
Rule 3 (uint8 inputs require non-negative limits to avoid “cannot do hardtanh on an unsigned type with negative limits”)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float, v_3 : float} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 5 then (0 ≤ v_2 ∧ 0 ≤ v_3)
>>
Rule 4 (min_val must not be greater than max_val)
{v_2 : float, v_3 : float} |= v_2 ≤ v_3
>>
Rule 5 (fp16 inputs require bounds within representable range to avoid “value cannot be converted to type at::Half without overflow”)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float, v_3 : float} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 6 then (-65504 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ 65504 ∧ -65504 ≤ v_3 ∧ v_3 ≤ 65504)
>>
Rule 6 (inplace flag is a well-formed boolean)
{v_4 : bool} |= v_4 = true ∨ v_4 = false
